# With the crown, the second sentence applies whether or not the "up to one target" was chosen: Target() chooses none,
# and neither of Bot2's two creatures may block either attacker, so Bot2 is never asked to declare blockers (bare
# refusal). Beside it, the scenario in which Aragorn's controller is not the monarch asks for blockers.

